WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:23.566
The children arrived at the castle and found Mabel's aunt reading a romance novel.

2
00:00:24.306 --> 00:00:28.067
"Excuse me," said Gerald, "I believe you've lost your niece."

3
00:00:28.087 --> 00:00:30.848
"I didn't lose Mabel.

4
00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:31.848
She left."

5
00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:34.313
"Did you get her note?"

6
00:00:34.713 --> 00:00:35.513
asked Kathleen.

7
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:39.956
"Yes, and I'm happy she's living with a rich lady."

8
00:00:41.016 --> 00:00:43.258
Jimmy couldn't be quiet a moment longer.

9
00:00:44.118 --> 00:00:46.019
He had to tell Mabel's aunt the truth.

10
00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:48.040
"Mabel's invisible!

11
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.041
She's standing right beside me."

12
00:00:50.061 --> 00:00:52.303
"Don't lie to me!"

13
00:00:52.723 --> 00:00:53.944
The aunt glared at Jimmy.

14
00:00:53.964 --> 00:00:56.625
"Please remove this boy.

15
00:00:57.005 --> 00:00:58.626
I'm quite happy about Mabel."

16
00:00:58.646 --> 00:01:01.768
"Well!" said Gerald.

17
00:01:02.708 --> 00:01:06.190
He was puzzled by this aunt who didn't care about her missing niece.

18
00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.671
"But what will Mabel's parents say?"

19
00:01:09.691 --> 00:01:14.473
"Mabel's parents are dead," the aunt said calmly.

20
00:01:15.494 --> 00:01:18.115
The children talked to Mabel's aunt for a few more minutes.

21
00:01:19.095 --> 00:01:21.956
She gave them permission to wander over the castle grounds.

22
00:01:23.197 --> 00:01:25.638
But she still didn't seem concerned about Mabel.

23
00:01:25.658 --> 00:01:30.240
"Good-bye, children," she said and went back to reading.

24
00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:36.062
When the children were outside again, Mabel said, "I knew she'd believe my note.

25
00:01:36.402 --> 00:01:38.283
She reads lots of romance novels.

26
00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:40.664
Strange things always happen in her books."

27
00:01:42.085 --> 00:01:44.526
Mabel suggested they walk to the Temple of Flora.

28
00:01:46.987 --> 00:01:52.049
When they were seated, she said, "I'm hungry, and you can't keep stealing food for me.

29
00:01:52.429 --> 00:01:54.630
I'll have to pretend to be a ghost in the castle."

30
00:01:54.650 --> 00:02:00.052
"You must stay with us until you can remove the ring," Kathleen said kindly.

31
00:02:01.348 --> 00:02:04.451
"I think we need to earn some money for food," said Mabel.

32
00:02:04.471 --> 00:02:06.413
"Let's go to the fair.

33
00:02:06.994 --> 00:02:08.915
Gerald can do magic tricks for money."

34
00:02:08.935 --> 00:02:11.258
"But I don't know any tricks!"

35
00:02:11.918 --> 00:02:12.639
said Gerald.

36
00:02:12.659 --> 00:02:15.061
"Don't worry," said Mabel.

37
00:02:15.081 --> 00:02:17.003
"I'm invisible.

38
00:02:17.023 --> 00:02:19.445
I can make it look like you're doing tricks."

39
00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.749
The fair was about half a mile away.

40
00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.012
Soon they could hear music from the carousel.

41
00:02:26.836 --> 00:02:31.499
Kathleen and Jimmy blended into the crowd while Gerald and Mabel stood in front of a tent.

42
00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:35.182
"Ladies and gentlemen," called out Gerald.

43
00:02:35.202 --> 00:02:39.325
"My invisible assistant can make money disappear."

44
00:02:40.646 --> 00:02:44.128
A crowd began to gather, and Kathleen and Jimmy joined in.

45
00:02:45.169 --> 00:02:47.271
Gerald laid nine pennies on the ground.

46
00:02:48.251 --> 00:02:51.554
Mabel picked them up and put them in her pocket to make them disappear.

47
00:02:53.395 --> 00:02:54.396
The audience clapped.

48
00:02:55.668 --> 00:02:59.871
"If you want to see more magic, I'll need to see more money," said Gerald.

49
00:03:00.732 --> 00:03:03.093
The audience dropped more coins onto the ground.

50
00:03:04.014 --> 00:03:05.895
Then Mabel made more things vanish.

51
00:03:06.876 --> 00:03:09.278
Other things appeared to move around by themselves.

52
00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.742
my final trick, I will vanish!"

53
00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.143
said Gerald.

54
00:03:18.104 --> 00:03:21.126
He stepped back, and Mabel wrapped her shawl around him.

55
00:03:22.867 --> 00:03:23.948
But nothing happened.

56
00:03:24.844 --> 00:03:25.704
"He can't do it!"

57
00:03:26.165 --> 00:03:26.905
someone yelled.

58
00:03:27.785 --> 00:03:29.506
The crowd pushed forward in anger.

59
00:03:29.526 --> 00:03:34.408
"I wish I could put you in my pocket," Mabel whispered to Gerald.

60
00:03:34.428 --> 00:03:36.509
"Then you'd be invisible."

61
00:03:37.129 --> 00:03:38.590
She squeezed her hands together.

62
00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.731
"Hey! The ring is loose!"

63
00:03:41.751 --> 00:03:43.392
"Come on!"

64
00:03:43.872 --> 00:03:45.292
shouted a man in the crowd.

65
00:03:45.312 --> 00:03:47.393
"We paid for a show."

66
00:03:48.754 --> 00:03:51.515
Gerald whispered to Mabel, "Go into the tent.

67
00:03:52.215 --> 00:03:54.116
Slip the ring under the canvas to me.

68
00:03:54.928 --> 00:03:59.109
When I see you in the crowd, I'll make myself disappear and catch up with you."

69
00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.470
Mabel did just that.

70
00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:07.812
"I'm back," she said to a surprised Kathleen and Jimmy.

71
00:04:07.832 --> 00:04:10.513
"Gerald's wearing the ring.

72
00:04:10.993 --> 00:04:12.074
Let's get out of here."

73
00:04:13.354 --> 00:04:18.696
As the children walked away, they heard Gerald announce, "Now I will vanish."

74
00:04:22.492 --> 00:04:26.996
Then the crowd roared, and the children knew he had really disappeared this time.

75
00:04:28.577 --> 00:04:32.520
After a few minutes, they heard footsteps on the road but saw no one.

76
00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:38.124
"Hello, I'm over here," said Gerald.

77
00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.646
"Good," said Mabel.

78
00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:42.627
"I want my ring back."

79
00:04:42.647 --> 00:04:45.910
"Well, you can't have it," Gerald answered.

80
00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.332
"Because I can't get it off!"
